__debug_bin
/db/misc
# fe/dist copied here for `go run main.go http` to serve directly without
# the full Dockerfile build - not part of the normal dev workflow, but
# harmless to ignore if it exists.
/dist
# Standardized local home for card-catalog data: one subfolder per set,
# named for whatever's being tracked, each holding {catalog.csv,set.json,
# images/} - exactly what `process-set --file --set-file --images-dir`
# needs, so re-running an import doesn't depend on re-locating files
# scattered across a scratchpad. Never committed - card images specifically
# shouldn't go to a public GitHub repo; may move to a separate private repo
# later. Lives on whichever machine actually runs process-set for now.
/sets

# One-off real credentials for running prod DB commands (e.g. migrations)
# manually from a laptop - never committed, see infra/envs/prod/.env.local.
/infra/envs/prod/

# Same "one-off real credentials, never committed" pattern as prod/.env.local
# above, but for real (e.g. prod eBay) credentials pointed at from local dev -
# infra/envs/local/.env itself IS committed (fake/non-secret defaults), this
# sibling file isn't.
/infra/envs/local/.env.local